        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The evidence that whey causes acne is thin: a few small case series, a plausible hormonal theory and no controlled trials. That is enough to justify a careful experiment if your skin worsened after you started a shake, and not enough to tell everyone to avoid whey. For that experiment, Naked Pea is our top pick, with NOW Sports Pea as the cheaper trial tub and Naked Egg as the closest like-for-like swap for whey.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Give any switch eight to twelve weeks, change nothing else, and keep your sugar low. If your acne is moderate, severe, painful or scarring, see a dermatologist now rather than waiting on a diet test; a protein swap can sit alongside real treatment but cannot replace it.
